Subject: [PATCH] load the staged conpty bundle from beside the executable

Translated from herdr's app-local ConPTY loader (Apache-2.0, commit
3150bd92; see NOTICE). Resolves an absolute candidate beside
current_exe, loads it with LoadLibraryExW restricted to the DLL's own
directory plus System32, and falls back to kernel32 cleanly when the
file is absent, unloadable or missing a symbol; a staged-but-unloadable
bundle keeps its reason for conpty_source() to report. Upstream 0.9
opened conpty.dll by bare name, letting the Windows DLL search order
(PATH, the current directory) decide what loaded into the process that
owns every pseudoconsole.

The bundle is all-or-nothing, in herdr's deployed layout: conpty/
conpty.dll and conpty/x64/OpenConsole.exe must both sit in the
executable's directory, a reparse point is rejected when the bundle is
checked - immediately before the load, not atomically with it, and a
hard link is not a reparse point - and other architectures never
consult a bundle (herdr's x86_64 gate). The crate has no logger;
conpty_source() reports the one-time choice for the daemon to surface
through its own log.

The manifest changes make cargo test -p portable-pty runnable: cargo
refuses to test a non-workspace package that declares
dev-dependencies, and the two declared here served only the
whoami_async example, whose declaration is dropped with them.
shared_library is dropped because the loader replaced its last use,
and the winapi libloaderapi feature covers LoadLibraryExW and friends.

Vendored base: portable-pty 0.9.0 plus 0003 and 0004.
